nantic_common
=============

Shared overrides and small cross-module customizations used by NaN-tic
modules.

Configuration
-------------

The ``TRYTOND_NANTIC_CONNECTION__WORKER_FUNCTIONS`` environment variable
restricts the functions that a queue worker may execute. Its value is a
pipe-separated list of ``model:method`` entries, for example::

    nantic.agent:run|nantic.chat.conversation:run_in_background

When the variable is defined, any queue entry whose function is not listed is
rejected at execution time. An empty value rejects every function. When the
variable is not defined, workers keep the unrestricted legacy behaviour.

